AGENCY AGREEMENT

This Agency Agreement (this "Agreement") is made as of March 29, 1999, by and between Biopure Corporation, a Delaware corporation (the "Company"), and the Agent named on the signature page (the "Agent").

WHEREAS, the Company is preparing to manufacture and sell Oxyglobin(R) brand veterinary products ("Products") enumerated on the Company's veterinary products agency price list (Exhibit A, as amended from time to time, the "Price List"); and
WHEREAS, the Agent and the Company wish to enter into an arrangement wherein the Agent will promote, sell, and collect payment for the Products as the Company's representative within the United States to duly licensed veterinarians ("Customers") on the terms herein;

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the premises and mutual covenants, the parties agree as follows:

1. APPOINTMENT AND ACCEPTANCE
1.1 Appointment. Subject to the terms herein, the Company appoints the Agent, and the Agent accepts appointment, as an authorized distributor agent within the Territory (defined in Section 1.2) to promote, sell, and collect payment for the Products to Customers. The Company may itself or appoint others to promote/sell/distribute the Products in the Territory.
1.2 Territory. The Territory is the 48 Continental United States (including DC) plus Alaska. The Agent is responsible for mutually agreed quarterly and annual sales objectives (per the "Business Plan") and will only earn compensation for sales within this Territory.
1.3 Business Plan. The parties will jointly develop a written Business Plan for each Contract Year (Nov 1 - Oct 31) during the Term, including sales/marketing strategies, financial projections, and Agent performance criteria. This Agreement governs in case of conflict with the Business Plan. The 1999 Contract Year Business Plan will be agreed upon within 30 days of the Agent Launch Date (or mutually agreed date); subsequent plans will be agreed upon at least 60 days prior to the Contract Year start. The parties will review and update the Business Plan quarterly. "Agent Launch Date" means the date the Company specifies in writing for the Agent to begin promoting/selling the Products (anticipated March 29, 1999).
1.4 Agent Obligations. At the Agent's sole expense (except as provided in the Business Plan), the Agent will:
(a) Meet performance criteria set forth in the Business Plan;
(b) Use reasonable best efforts to market/promote the Products in the Territory (via direct sales calls, advertising, etc.) in accordance with the Business Plan or the Company's written approval;
(c) Immediately forward to the Company's Technical Service Department (in mutually agreed format) all complaints/inquiries relating to Product safety, quality, packaging, or customer satisfaction (excluding inquiries about availability, pricing, billing, or delivery) from Customers/consumers in the Territory, and all inquiries from outside the Territory;
(d) Maintain a suitable staff in the Territory to properly promote/sell the Products and ensure customer satisfaction;
(e) Not solicit/accept orders from Customers outside the Territory (after the Agent Launch Date) or distribute/resell Products outside the Territory or to non-licensed veterinarians;
(f) Meet with the Company at least quarterly (starting with the Agent Launch Date quarter) to review activities, providing sales volume, efforts, and other mutually agreed information;
(g) Submit all non-Company-provided sales/promotion/training materials to the Company for review at least 30 days prior to use, consider Company comments, and obtain express written consent (not unreasonably withheld) before use;
(h) Make field sales personnel available for at least 4 hours of initial training and telesales personnel for 1 hour of initial training (plus supplemental training as the Company deems appropriate) at mutually agreed times/locations;
(i) Make field sales representatives available to work with the Company's field sales representatives for at least 2 full business days per Contract Year;
(j) Maintain Product sales to meet or exceed the previous year's annual sales in the same competitive environment;
(k) Cooperate in national/area promotional programs offered by the Company;
(l) Follow the Company's credit policy (Section 2.3) and evaluate Customer creditworthiness. Products shipped to Customers will be billed to the Agent at the current price list/promotional price minus a 10% discount (Section 1.5(d)). The Agent accepts full responsibility for Customer payment upon transmitting orders to the Company;
(m) Transmit Customer orders to the Company at least once daily (via fax, email, or agreed means) to ensure timely processing/shipping;
(n) Sell Products only at the Company's current list or promotional price.
1.5 Company Obligations. At the Company's sole expense (except as provided in the Business Plan), the Company will:
(a) Use reasonable best efforts to fill/ship accepted orders daily (no later than the next business day; orders received on Fridays/holiday eves ship the next business day unless special arrangements are made at the Customer's expense). The Company will provide a shipment confirmation list to the Agent by the end of the next business day. For backorders, the Company will inform the Agent and ship inventory fairly; available products will be shipped on a first-come, first-served basis (partial shipments for large orders at the Company's discretion). The Company will not provide Products exceeding 120% of the maximum quantity specified in the Business Plan;
(b) Provide initial training (4 hours for field sales, 1 hour for telesales) and supplemental training as appropriate at mutually agreed times/locations;
(c) Supply literature, ad reprints, and other promotional aids to assist in Product sales;
(d) Compensate the Agent with a 10% total discount off the current/promotional price (8% to the Agent, 2% to the Agent's sales representatives) based on monthly units shipped (excluding taxes, shipping, and handling). The Company will also pay a quarterly 2% incentive commission (1% to the Agent, 1% to the sales force) upon meeting mutually agreed quarterly goals (Exhibit B). Unmet quarterly goals will be eligible for the incentive if annual goals are met (paid at fiscal year-end);
(e) Replace any Product that is outdated (by no more than 90 days) with equal Product.

2. PRODUCTS PURCHASE AND SALE
2.1 Orders. Customer orders taken by the Agent are subject to the Company's acceptance (not binding until accepted). The Company may accept/reject orders in whole or in part. All orders ship in minimum quantities of one box (two bags).
2.2 Prices. Prices are as set forth in Exhibit A (current Price List). The Agent may not deviate from Company-specified pricing. Prices are F.O.B. the Customer's facility, exclusive of taxes/duties. The Company will provide at least 10 days' prior written notice of price changes; orders are invoiced at the price in effect when the Company receives the order.
2.3 Payment Terms. The Agent will pay the Company for Products shipped to Customers within 30 days of the statement date (45 days if paying via electronic funds transfer). Payments are in U.S. Dollars without set-off or deduction for taxes/duties.
2.4 Taxes. The Customer bears all taxes/duties on Product purchases (excluding taxes on the Company's income). The Company bears taxes/duties incidental to Product production. The Company will provide necessary documents to implement this provision.
2.5 Claims. Claims for delivery shortages must be made within 10 business days of the Customer's receipt of shipment. See Exhibit C ("General Information") for sales, shipping, and return policies.
2.6 Warranty. The Company warrants that Products shipped to Customers: (a) are merchantable and commercially salable; (b) have a remaining shelf life of at least 12 months; and (c) are manufactured, labeled, packaged, handled, stored, and shipped in compliance with applicable laws. The Customer's exclusive remedy for breach is replacement of non-conforming Product (freight prepaid). The Company is not liable for incidental/consequential damages. Claims must be submitted in accordance with the Company's published bulletins (as amended). THE COMPANY MAKES NO OTHER WARRANTIES (EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE). Statements by Company representatives do not constitute warranties.

3. COVENANTS
3.1 Purchaser Guarantees, Instructions. The Agent will not furnish any guarantees/warranties or use instructions for the Products to third parties except as approved in writing by the Company or as stated on Product labeling/Company-provided materials.
3.2 Trademarks. The Agent will promote/sell the Products only under the Company's registered trademarks, copyrights, brand names, or product names ("Trademarks") as authorized in writing. The Agent acquires no interest in the Trademarks and will not use them for non-Company Products. The Agent will immediately cease using Trademarks upon Agreement expiration/termination.
3.3 Insurance. Each party will maintain commercial general liability and umbrella liability insurance (including product liability) with reputable insurers, in amounts customary for similar businesses (minimum $5,000,000 combined single limit per occurrence/aggregate). The Agent's policy will name the Company as an additional insured; the Company's policy will name the Agent as an additional insured. Each policy will provide at least 30 days' prior written notice of cancellation/modification. Each party will furnish a Certificate of Insurance upon request.
3.4 Notice of Certain Events. The Agent will promptly notify the Company of: alleged Trademark infringement by third parties; alleged infringement of others' proprietary rights; Product liability claims; and any event materially adverse to Product sales/distribution in the Territory.
3.5 Indemnification.
(a) The Agent will indemnify the Company (and its officers, directors, employees, agents, affiliates) against all losses, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees, a "Loss") arising from: (i) the Agent's breach of representations/warranties/obligations; or (ii) the Agent's violation of this Agreement, law, or other duties in connection with Product promotion/sale/collection. The Agent is not liable for incidental/consequential damages.
(b) The Company will indemnify the Agent (and its officers, directors, employees, agents, affiliates) against any Loss arising from the Company's breach of representations/warranties/obligations.
(c) The notifying party will promptly notify the indemnifying party of third-party claims ("Third Party Claims") and provide a reasonable opportunity to defend (at the indemnifying party's expense). If the indemnifying party fails to defend within 30 days, the notifying party may defend/settle (exercising reasonable judgment) at the indemnifying party's expense (with prior written approval, not unreasonably withheld). Each party will provide reasonable assistance in the defense.
3.6 Assistance with Claims. Each party will furnish reasonable assistance to the other in defending third-party claims related to Product manufacture/distribution/sale/use, at the requesting party's expense.
3.7 Confidential Information and Publicity. Each party will use the other's confidential information ("Confidential Information") solely for this Agreement and not disclose it to third parties (except employees/consultants bound by similar nondisclosure obligations) without prior written consent. Neither party will disclose the Agreement's terms or use the other's name in advertising/promotions/press releases without prior written consent (except as required by law or to enforce rights). Confidential Information means non-public information belonging to a party (excluding information public through no fault of the receiving party, received from a third party with lawful right, known prior to disclosure, or independently developed). This Section survives Agreement expiration/termination.

4. TERM AND TERMINATION
4.1 Term. This Agreement is effective as of the date first written above and continues until terminated pursuant to Section 4.2.
4.2 Termination. This Agreement may be terminated as follows:
(a) Automatically if either party materially breaches its obligations (including Agent performance criteria) and fails to remedy within 30 days (5 business days for payment defaults) of written notice;
(b) By the Company upon written notice if there is a material change in the Agent's organization, ownership, management, or control (Agent will promptly notify the Company of such events);
(c) By either party without cause after January 31, 1999, upon at least 90 days' prior written notice;
(d) By either party if the parties fail to agree on a Business Plan for a Contract Year before its start (30 days' prior written notice);
(e) By the Company upon at least 5 days' prior written notice if publicity concerning the Agent materially harms the Agent's or Products' reputation;
(f) By the Company upon at least 90 days' prior written notice if it terminates, sells, or transfers its veterinary products business in full.
4.3 Effect of Termination. Upon termination:
(a) The Agent will immediately discontinue representing itself as the Company's agent and cease all Product-related activities;
(b) All amounts owed by either party become immediately due and payable (per Section 2.3);
(c) Unfulfilled orders may be completed by the Company or transferred to another Agent. Termination does not prejudice pre-termination rights/obligations. Neither party is liable for special/consequential damages. Sections 3.5, 3.6, 3.7, and this Section 4.3 survive termination.

5. MISCELLANEOUS
5.1 Notices. All notices are in writing and delivered by personal service, overnight courier, telecommunication, or registered U.S. Mail to the recipient's address on the signature page. Notices are effective upon: (a) actual receipt; (b) next business day (courier); (c) next business day (telecommunication, with confirmation); or (d) 5 business days (registered mail). Either party may change its address by written notice.
5.2 Assignment. This Agreement binds and benefits the parties' successors and permitted assigns. Neither party may assign rights/obligations without the other's prior written consent.
5.3 Waivers. Waivers of rights must be in writing and do not constitute continuing waivers of other breaches.
5.4 Relationship of Parties. This Agreement does not create a joint venture, partnership, or agency (except as expressly provided). The Agent is an independent contractor and has no authority to bind the Company.
5.5 Force Majeure. Neither party is liable for delays/failure to perform due to causes beyond its reasonable control (e.g., acts of God, fire, strikes, floods, transportation delays, inability to obtain raw materials). The affected party will promptly notify the other and use reasonable efforts to minimize delays.
5.6 Governing Law; Jurisdiction. This Agreement is governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts (excluding conflict of law principles). Massachusetts courts have non-exclusive jurisdiction over disputes. Service of process may be made by registered mail.
5.7 Amendments. This Agreement may only be amended by a written instrument signed by both parties.
5.8 Remedies. Remedies for breach are cumulative and may be exercised concurrently or separately.
5.9 Severability. If any provision is invalid/unenforceable, it will be replaced to achieve the original purpose (if possible), and the remainder of the Agreement remains in effect. If the fundamental objectives cannot be achieved without the invalid provision, either party may terminate without penalty.
5.10 Interest. Overdue amounts bear interest at 2% above Citibank's prime rate (or the maximum permitted by law) from the due date to payment.
5.11 Miscellaneous. Each party bears its own expenses for negotiating/preparing/executing this Agreement. Headings are for convenience and not part of the Agreement. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts (each deemed an original). This Agreement supersedes all prior oral/written agreements concerning the subject matter.

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above.

